---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const jsonLd = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "ProfilePage", "mainEntity": {"@type": "Person", "name": "Arbaz Siddiqui", "jobTitle": "Principal Software Engineer", "worksFor": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Turnip", "url": "https://zaps.design/"}, "url": "https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me", "email": "mailto:arbaz00@gmail.com", "sameAs": ["https://github.com/arbazsiddiqui", "https://huggingface.co/arbazsiddiqui", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/arbazsiddiqui"], "knowsAbout": ["AI infrastructure", "distributed systems", "LLM fine-tuning", "RAG", "Kubernetes", "Go", "Node.js", "Kafka", "MQTT", "WebSockets", "RTMP", "FFmpeg", "live streaming", "real-time systems", "Redis", "Postgres", "Neo4j", "Elasticsearch", "Docker", "content automation", "cryptocurrency exchanges", "blockchain", "trading engines", "DeFi"]}};
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="About Arbaz Siddiqui, a software engineer with nine years of experience in distributed systems, now building AI infrastructure and shipping products end to end."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="narrow section">
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>

    <div class="prose bio">
      <p>
        I'm Arbaz. I write backends, and for nine years the thing I've been
        good at is the part users never see. Streams that stay under five
        seconds, queues that don't drop, payments that reconcile, clusters
        that hold when traffic triples overnight. At
        <a href="/about">Turnip</a> I was the only backend engineer for two
        years and took it to 25M users. Before that I built ticketing for one
        of India's biggest event platforms, and a crypto exchange with a
        matching engine and wallets across six chains.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since 2024 the work has moved to AI models and what surrounds them.
        GPU inference, fine-tuning, retrieval, and pipelines that run with
        nobody watching. I learn it by shipping it, so this year I released
        <a href="/ozan">a language model</a>, built
        <a href="/footnote">a media channel that runs itself</a>, and put
        <a href="/projects">apps</a> on the App Store.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="room-label worklog-head">Work</h2>

    <div class="job">
      <div class="job-head">
        <h3><a href="https://zaps.design/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Turnip</a></h3>
        <p class="medium-line">Principal Software Engineer, January 2021 to present</p>
      </div>
      <p class="prose">
        One startup, four pivots: mobile-game streaming, Clubhouse-style
        live audio, a creator social network, and now Zaps, an AI design
        suite.
      </p>
      <ul class="jb">
        <li>Grew the backend from nothing to 25M users, twenty-one services on Kubernetes behind Kong, with Kafka and Redis carrying the load.</li>
        <li>Built the game-streaming stack first, RTMP and FFmpeg ingest running 50K streams a day at under five seconds of latency.</li>
        <li>Then the live audio rooms on Agora, where MQTT and Firebase kept every listener's state in sync for 2M people a month across 70M minutes of calls.</li>
        <li>Gave the social app a feed that surfaced people worth following, second-degree discovery over a Neo4j graph, indexed in real time by Elasticsearch on an event-driven Kafka core.</li>
        <li>Brought AI photo editing into the product, face swap, retouch and background tools on ComfyUI, orchestrated with LangGraph and later n8n on Kubernetes.</li>
        <li>Cut GPU spend by 80% by moving generation onto a distributed GPU network while still returning images in about two seconds, and another 70% off infrastructure with autoscaling and serverless.</li>
        <li>Made the template library searchable by meaning rather than by tag, RAG over every design and carousel with LangChain.</li>
        <li>Built an engineering platform that let ten product people ship 17 internal tools without a single engineer commit.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="job">
      <div class="job-head">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/mouse-belt/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MouseBelt</a></h3>
        <p class="medium-line">Senior Backend Engineer, April 2020 to January 2021</p>
      </div>
      <p class="prose">
        A centralized cryptocurrency exchange, and the crypto work around it.
      </p>
      <ul class="jb">
        <li>Built the exchange backend. Accounts, KYC, sessions, markets, order flow, fee schedules, referral commissions, API keys with IP allowlists, and failover.</li>
        <li>Worked on the low-latency core, a matching engine written in C with its own HTTP and WebSocket access layers, market price feeds, and trade history services.</li>
        <li>Multi-chain custody. Deposits and withdrawals across Bitcoin, Ethereum, EOS, Cosmos, ICON, and Binance Chain.</li>
        <li>Built a multi-chain DEX aggregator with price scrapers across BSC, ICON, and Moonbeam, plus a blockchain indexer for on-chain history.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="job">
      <div class="job-head">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/insiderdotin" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Paytm Insider</a></h3>
        <p class="medium-line">Lead Backend Engineer, 2017 to April 2020</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="jb">
        <li>Led the team behind movie ticketing that held 500+ requests a second on sale nights without a glitch.</li>
        <li>Designed the logistics architecture. Delivery opt-in, order tracking, and the internal tools for managing shipments.</li>
        <li>Built the full e-commerce flow. Cart, payments, inventory, and taxation.</li>
        <li>Ran it all as AWS microservices on Kubernetes, with serverless functions on Lambda and Kinesis carrying the on-demand work.</li>
        <li>Led a team of 7 and interviewed 100+ engineers for backend and DevOps roles.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="job">
      <div class="job-head">
        <h3><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/ithaka---experience-it-all/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ithaka</a></h3>
        <p class="medium-line">Intern, 2016 to 2017</p>
      </div>
      <p class="prose">
        A travel-planning startup, and my first real-time systems work:
        built its omni-channel chat server bridging the app, Facebook
        Messenger, and support agents over Socket.IO and Firebase, with
        conversation handoff and Elasticsearch-backed search.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="job">
      <div class="job-head">
        <h3><a href="https://provakil.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Provakil</a></h3>
        <p class="medium-line">Intern, 2016</p>
      </div>
      <p class="prose">
        Legal-tech. Wrote scrapers and fetchers that pulled daily cause
        lists from Indian courts, including the Delhi High Court and the
        national consumer courts, into structured case data.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="room-label worklog-head">Now</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Right now I build as an indie dev, which means the whole thing and
        not just the code. Idea, product, distribution, growth. Day to day
        the work is automation pipelines, pushing language, diffusion and
        retrieval models to see how cheaply they can run unattended before
        the quality gives out. None of it is a demo. Every project is live,
        with real users and real numbers.
      </p>
    </div>

  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-title { margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .bio { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1.12rem; }
  .worklog-head { margin-top: 2.6rem; }
  .job + .job { margin-top: 2.4rem; }
  .job-head h3 { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.018em; }
  .job-head h3 a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .job-head h3 a:hover { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; }
  .medium-line { font-style: italic; color: var(--soft); margin-top: 0.15rem; }
  .job-head { margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
  .jb { padding-left: 1.25rem; margin-top: 0.8rem; }
  .jb li + li { margin-top: 0.7rem; }
  .jb li::marker { color: var(--accent); }
  .job .prose { font-size: 1.05rem; }
</style>
